# Running heads (reference/common/references.md): page of 300 × 200 with margins of 20, page area of 260 × 160 from
# (20, 20). Lines of 12 (Size 10); with the test metrics each character measures 5 pt. The header writes {heading 1},
# the last Heading 1 that has started on the page or before, anchored to the left and as wide as its text (Offset with
# auto on the right): y = 20 − 15 = 5. The footer writes {heading 1: first}, the first Heading 1 that starts on the
# page or, if none does, the same as {heading 1}, anchored to the right: its right edge is at 280 and its bottom edge at
# 180 + 15 = 195, so y = 183. Both are laid out on each page with the text of that page.
#   Page 1: intro fills the page; no heading has started: both texts are empty, with no lines, 0 × 0.
#   Page 2: Uno (12) and uno (148). Header and footer "Uno": 15 wide.
#   Page 3: Dos (12) and the first 148 of dos. Both "Dos": 15 wide.
#   Page 4: the other 160 of dos. No heading starts: both keep "Dos".
#   Page 5: Tres (12), tres (20), Cuatro (12) and cuatro (30). Header "Cuatro" (30 wide, the last); footer "Tres"
#     (20 wide, the first of the page): x = 280 − 20 = 260.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
	Section:
		Page overlay:
			Id: head
			Offset: -15 auto auto 0
			Text: {heading 1}
				Id: head-text
		Page overlay:
			Id: foot
			Offset: auto 0 -15 auto
			Text: {heading 1: first}
				Id: foot-text
		Block:
			Id: intro
			Box:
				Height: 160
		Heading 1:
			Id: h-uno
			Text: Uno
		Block:
			Id: uno
			Box:
				Height: 148
		Heading 1:
			Id: h-dos
			Text: Dos
		Block:
			Id: dos
			Box:
				Height: 308
		Heading 1:
			Id: h-tres
			Text: Tres
		Block:
			Id: tres
			Box:
				Height: 20
		Heading 1:
			Id: h-cuatro
			Text: Cuatro
		Block:
			Id: cuatro
			Box:
				Height: 30
